# Inspector #54 optional-inline-budget launch review

**Review mode:** independent prospective Spec/Standards review, read-only. I inspected `docs/check-policy.md`, `CODING_STANDARDS.md`, the inspector54 README/RESULT/CANDIDATE/patch, the candidate launch packet, all three role plans, the existing `development-v2.py` runner, and the guarded source activation script. I did not activate sources or execute the candidate, runner, backend, hooks, or preflight.

## Verdict

**CONDITIONAL PASS for a bounded diagnostic launch; no unconditional launch approval and no adoption or stock credit.**

The candidate is an exact pristine compiler copy plus the reviewed optional-inline patch, and the role plans bind the complete 53-source ordinary consumer, existing runner, tools, environment, CPU/caps, and 207,834-byte independent oracle. Launch remains gated on an outer coordinator that actually performs the declared source activation, post-activation preflight, serialized role sequence, and unconditional restoration. The `sourceActivation` field is metadata: `development-v2.py` does not invoke it.

